From cdf50f7a5281bfa2023588496cca2f0c25e84912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] workaround: clk: mediatek: retain firmware-owned MT6897 mux
 state

Provide topckgen and VLP clocks while leaving hardware-voter and VCP-owned
muxes read-only. Their firmware ownership protocol is not implemented.
The restriction is integral to these controller definitions; keep it explicit.

Original-Commit: local development history
Original-Author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Original-Date: 2026-10-16T16:22:00+08:00
Original-Commit: local development history
Original-Author: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Original-Date: 2026-10-20T02:41:23+08:00
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897-topckgen.c | 1576 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897-vlpckgen.c |  408 +++++
 2 files changed, 1984 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897-topckgen.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/clk/mediatek/clk-mt6897-vlpckgen.c

